End an open SysEx when a status byte interrupts it.

Only System Real-Time may appear inside a SysEx (M2-104-UM 7.7.1). Any other status
byte ends it. bytestreamParse() only acted on SYSEX_START and SYSEX_STOP, so
sysex7State stayed set and every following data byte was appended to the SysEx
accumulator instead of being parsed:

    F0 11 22 90 3C 7F 90 3E 7F
    was: 30161122 3C7F3E7F   - one SysEx that swallowed both notes
    now: 30021122 00000000, 20903C7F, 20903E7F

When a late F7 does arrive the note data has already leaked into the payload, and a
device that never sends one silences all subsequent traffic. This is the same
malformed-input family as the inMusic case in issue #39.

The second F0 case is the same defect seen from the other side. SYSEX_START called
dumpSysex7State(true), which emits the abandoned fragment with its current state, so a
fragment was labelled Start and the following message Complete. A receiver reassembling
that pair produces one merged payload:

    F0 11 12 F0 31 32 33 34 F7
    was: 30121112 00000000, 30043132 33340000   - Start with no End, then Complete
    now: 30021112 00000000, 30043132 33340000   - two independent complete messages

endSysex7State() emits nothing when no data has accumulated, so an immediately repeated
F0 is still ignored, and dumpSysex7State() is left alone because callers rely on it to
flush a partial SysEx while deliberately staying in the SysEx state.

Upstream: https://github.com/midi2-dev/AM_MIDI2.0Lib/issues/39#issuecomment-5258615978

diff --git a/include/bytestreamToUMP.h b/include/bytestreamToUMP.h
--- a/include/bytestreamToUMP.h
+++ b/include/bytestreamToUMP.h
@@ -116,6 +116,30 @@
 			return mess;
 		}
 
+		// Close a SysEx that a status byte has interrupted, per M2-104-UM 7.7.1. Nothing is
+		// emitted when no data has accumulated, so a repeated F0 is simply ignored.
+		void endSysex7State() {
+			if (sysex7State == 0) {
+				return;
+			}
+
+			if (sysex7State == 1 && sysex7Pos == 0) {
+				sysex7State = 0;
+				return;
+			}
+
+			umpMess[writeIndex] = ((UMP_SYSEX7 << 4) + defaultGroup + 0L) << 24;
+			umpMess[writeIndex] +=  ((sysex7State == 1?0:3) + 0L) << 20;
+			umpMess[writeIndex] +=  ((sysex7Pos + 0L) << 16);
+			umpMess[writeIndex] += (sysex[0] << 8) + sysex[1];
+			increaseWrite();
+			umpMess[writeIndex] = ((sysex[2] + 0L) << 24) + ((sysex[3] + 0L)<< 16) + (sysex[4] << 8) + sysex[5];
+			increaseWrite();
+			sysex7State = 0;
+			sysex7Pos = 0;
+			M2Utils::clear(sysex, 0, sizeof(sysex));
+		}
+
 		void dumpSysex7State(bool reset) {
 			if (sysex7State > 0 && sysex7Pos > 0) {
 				//Then dump current bytes
@@ -151,7 +175,9 @@
 				d0 = midi1Byte;
 				d1 = 255;
 				if (midi1Byte == SYSEX_START){
-					dumpSysex7State(true);
+					endSysex7State();
+					sysex7State = 1;
+					sysex7Pos = 0;
 				}
                 else if (midi1Byte == SYSEX_STOP){
